# Hi Roshan!

You=E2=80=99re confirmed for this week=E2=80=99s **ASU AIR Spark Challenge*=
*, hosted by Knowledge Enterprise Research Technology Office and Enterprise=
 Technology. In this **virtual, 2-day hackathon**, you'll work in **teams o=
f 3-4** members to explore any use case with supercharged AI compute, then =
get ready to take the virtual stage to pitch your creation to an expert jur=
y for grand prizes. Read on for important details like parking, team format=
ions, prize details and more!

_**IMPORTANT: The information below is exclusive to individuals who have co=
nfirmed their program acceptance. DO NOT SHARE WITH OTHERS.**_

## Challenge resources
**Before Spark Challenge start:** To hit the ground running at the ASU AIR =
Spark Challenge, get prepared with the information and tools you need:
* Learn Git at [https://swcarpentry.github.io/git-novice/](https://swcarpen=
try.github.io/git-novice/). Git will be used to make sure you and your team=
 can build your code collaboratively, and the judges will be using your Git=
hub link to check out your results!
* Get your API key and get started with AIR at [https://docs.rc.asu.edu/ai/=
getting-started](https://docs.rc.asu.edu/ai/getting-started). Getting your =
tool of choice, API key, and some experience ahead of time will make sure y=
ou're ready as soon as the clock starts.
* Watch a recording of our recent [AI Research Platform workshop](https://a=
su.zoom.us/rec/share/c0YGNrlZWQHZB4AL6JaREYVSg6J6k9MZ0pJ39511Sh8x5dRLi8jfXq=
5AGcOD0rzc.8Valg6wF1Alfwsbd), led by Knowledge Enterprise Research Technolo=
gy Office
## Spark Challenge schedule
**Wed, Sept. 2, 5:00-7:30 p.m.=C2=A0 | Challenge launch, Zoom**
Link: [https://asu.zoom.us/j/87410584863](https://asu.zoom.us/j/87410584863=
)
Challenge kickoff! Join us online to explore the challenge brief, access ch=
allenge resources and network together before teams begin working.=C2=A0
**Thurs, Sept. 3=C2=A0 | Hacking and mentorship, Online**
Teams work together, checking in remotely with challenge organizers and men=
tors from Knowledge Enterprise Research Technology Office by appointment.=
=C2=A0
**Thurs, Sept. 3, 11:59 p.m. | Submissions due, Online**
Teams finalize and upload their solutions; submissions due by 11:59 p.m.=C2=
=A0
**Fri, Sept. 4, 10:00 a.m.-1:30 p.m. | Closing ceremony**
[RSVP for the finale](https://asu.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_tUH5IaKFRaW8u=
QGPBYGuww)
Grand finale: demos, pitches, awards! Join us on Zoom as teams pitch live, =
demo solutions and answer jury Q&A to determine top awarded teams. Share th=
e webinar RSVP link with colleagues, friends and family!
## Teaming
**If you applied solo**, we=E2=80=99ll pair you with other solo applicants =
based on experience and skill level. You will be introduced to your team on=
 Sept. 2, 2026. Our goal is to create balanced, high-performing groups. Tea=
ms are strategically assembled based on:
* Technical skill level: Balancing expertise across the group.
* Academic diversity: Mixing backgrounds for broader perspective.
* Experience: Accounting for prior Hackathon and tool use
* Availability: Ensuring that overall availability is factored into the tea=
m=E2=80=99s structure so that progress remains steady.
**If you applied with a team**, please [confirm your team lineup and confir=
mation status](https://airtable.com/appzNHpLL8HIkEFLA/shrK3BdKVYTouy3wp). R=
eminder that any unconfirmed spots may be released to any Waitlisted regist=
rants. Email [et-hackathons@asu.edu](mailto:et-hackathons@asu.edu) with any=
 needs.
## Prize pool
**=F0=9F=8F=86 Grand prize $1,000** Awarded to the top team as determined b=
y our expert jury panel using a standard rubric.
**=E2=AD=90 Fan Favorite $500** Voted on and awarded by your fellow competi=
ng teams for their favorite use case.

Awards are sponsored by the Knowledge Enterprise Research Technology Office=
 and issued courtesy of Enterprise Technology. Student prizes will be credi=
ted as account scholarships; staff/faculty prizes will be issued as stipend=
s.

Please email [et-hackathons@asu.edu](mailto:et-hackathons@asu.edu) with any=
 questions or needs prior to the hack. We look forward to seeing you at the=
 Spark Challenge, September 2, starting at 5:00 PM!

# Forks up!=20
